{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CggHCHvtnDH8Ghv21Lcr4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is in `money.py`. `split_cents` now spreads the remainder one grosz at a time across the first few shares, so the shares always add up to the total.\n\n```python\nshare, remainder = divmod(total, people)\nreturn [share + 1 if i < remainder else share for i in range(people)]\n```\n\nI ran a quick check and got these results:\n- `split_cents(100, 3)` returns `[34, 33, 33]`, which sums to 100.\n- `split_cents(100, 4)` returns `[25, 25, 25, 25]`.\n- `split_cents(2, 5)` returns `[1, 1, 0, 0, 0]`.\n- `split_cents(0, 3)` returns `[0, 0, 0]`.\n- The shares for `split_cents(101, 7)` sum to 101.\n\nThe first person in the split gets the extra grosz. If you want a different rule, such as a random person or the payer, say so. I didn't commit anything.\n\nThe bash startup printed a `.bashrc: Permission denied` warning, which is a sandbox quirk and didn't affect the check."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":536,"cache_read_input_tokens":17853,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":536},"output_tokens":351,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05d91bb1-6874-4daf-b73a-ffeb6702da81","uuid":"a24cf1a6-f993-417b-9c2f-c7f208c794ee","timestamp":"2026-11-03T16:05:28.749Z","request_id":"req_011CggHCHgWAVA7bFMCZytez"}
